import type { Catalog } from './i18n';

/**
 * German: every English text of the game (see i18n.ts) and its translation.
 *
 * The Host is addressed informally ("du") everywhere, in the UI and by every voice.
 *
 * Names are never translated: the people (Nicole, Rask, Pim, Hedda Kroll, the pilots), the ships (Magpie,
 * Patience, Lot 7731, the Sovereign), the sponsors, their products and the places' proper names
 * (Psyche) stay as in English; a place named by a plain word (the Boneyard: der Schrottplatz, an arena's title)
 * is translated; a pun on a name is
 * explained beside it instead ("Magpie. Wie die Elster: …").
 *
 * Glossary (English → German), kept the same in every text:
 * - Host → Host (pl. Hosts); clone → Klon (pl. Klone); pilot → Pilot; training clones → Übungsklone
 * - Solar Coins → Solar Coins; hangar → Hangar; upgrade → Upgrade; looks → Optik
 * - Human / Alien Interceptor → Menschen- / Alien-Abfangjäger; The Sovereign → die Sovereign (a ship's name, kept; the label alone: Sovereign)
 * - Deathmatch → Deathmatch; Race → Rennen; Last Clone Standing → Der letzte Klon; Capture the Flag → Capture the Flag;
 *   The President's Fleet → Die Flotte des Präsidenten; every mode in turn → alle Modi im Wechsel
 * - round → Runde; lap → Runde (a race's lap; sentences that hold both keep them apart by context); gate → Tor;
 *   ring → Ring; coil → Spule; start / finish → Start / Ziel; best lap → Bestzeit
 * - flight school → Flugschule; course → Kurs; drill → Übung; Basic training → Grundausbildung; Racer → Rennpilot;
 *   Gladiator → Gladiator; Arsenal → Arsenal; Tactician → Taktiker
 * - flight computer → Bordcomputer; Nicole's pet names, one per English one: darling → Schätzchen,
 *   love → Liebling, sweetheart → Schatz, honey → Süßer, my hero → mein (großer) Held,
 *   big guy → Großer, handsome → mein Hübscher
 * - announcer → Kommentator; the Orange President → der Orange Präsident; United Solar States → Vereinigte Sonnenstaaten;
 *   Ministry of War → Kriegsministerium; Presidential Games → Präsidentenspiele; Rockborn → Rockborn (a people's name, kept: die Rockborn);
 *   Solar Wall → Sonnenmauer; sponsor → Sponsor; sponsor break / ad → Werbung
 * - main drive → Hauptantrieb; drive → Antrieb; thrusters → Steuerdüsen; brake → Bremse / bremsen; burn → Schub;
 *   flip → Wende / wenden; dodge → Ausweichen; fine aim → Feinzielen; autopilot → Autopilot; free drift → freier Drift;
 *   overdrive → Overdrive (der Overdrive; English terms of the game stay English, as the laser is the Laser)
 * - laser → Laser; heat → Hitze; radiators → Kühler; armor → Panzerung; plating → Panzerplatten; hull → Rumpf (its shell: hits, paint, clamps), but the own ship as a whole (hull 7731, the hull the dock takes) → Jäger
 * - torpedo → Torpedo (pl. Torpedos); torpedo tubes → Torpedorohre; lock → Zielerfassung; hook → Haken; harpoon → Harpune;
 *   cable → Seil; winch → Winde; probe → Sonde; sealed probe → versiegelte Sonde; twin laser → Zwillingslaser;
 *   repair → Reparatur; nova core → Nova-Kern
 * - battleship → Schlachtschiff; battery → Batterie; reactor → Reaktor; drive plume → Antriebsstrahl
 * - side → Seite; Orange / Blue → Orange / Blau; base → Basis; core → Kern; sponsor core → Sponsorkern
 * - solar flare → Sonneneruption; field → Feld; deep space → tiefes All; arena → Arena
 * - kill → Abschuss; deaths → Tode; score → Punkte (pts → Pkt.); standings → Wertung; callsign → Rufzeichen;
 *   dogfight → Duell; crosshair → Fadenkreuz; marker → Markierung; live link → Live-Verbindung
 * - neon trim → Neonstreifen; drive flame → Antriebsflamme; aim / reflexes / daring → Zielen / Reflexe / Wagemut
 * - classes Cruise / Pro / Max → Locker / Profi / Max
 * - ping → Ping (the gamer term, kept)
 *
 * Spoken lines (the flight computer's and the announcer's) write numbers and units out in words, so the voice reads them
 * well. The announcer's bot names stay lowercase: they are the keys of their rendered clips.
 */
